title: what atoms are, and how to bounadry them
pid: e42e2cd5-5ae0-4072-b73a-a633cee08e4b
body: |2-
  Others may have written about this better than me.
  Andy Matuschak has written about defining atoms.

  It's kind of xen.
  Don't let that put you off; it doesn't need to be done perfectly.
  Just define some and process them; it will be powerful.

  Atoms are atomic expressions.
  They are the written subset of
  the things that will be available to think about.

  Atoms are individual words or collections of words.
  They can stand on their own,
  but will also stand in relation to each other.
